<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guaram I of Iberia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/590">590</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guaram I was the first presiding prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, chosen by the nobility in 588 with Byzantine backing after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a> had abolished the Iberian monarchy. He held the Byzantine title of kouropalates and founded the Guaramid line, which shared the office of presiding prince with the Chosroid family over the following two centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guaram-i-of-iberia.jpg" alt="Guaram I of Iberia" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: American Numismatic Society · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kartvelo-Sasanian_coin_of_Gurgen_i.e._Guaram_I_of_Iberia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 588 the nobility, with Byzantine support, chose <b>Guaram I</b> as presiding prince, beginning the Principality of Iberia, and Georgian kingship was restored only in the ninth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-iberia">Kingdom of Iberia · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 588, with Byzantine backing, <b>Guaram I</b> of the Guaramid family was recognised as presiding prince, holding the Byzantine title of kouropalates, and the office passed among leading families for three centuries.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-iberia">Principality of Iberia</a></li></ul></section>
